---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import InfoPage from '../components/InfoPage.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Flights — Ben & Caitlin · Bermuda 2027" description="How to get to Bermuda for Ben & Caitlin's wedding in June 2027.">
  <InfoPage
    heading="Getting There"
    subheading="Flights to Bermuda"
    intro="Getting to Bermuda is surprisingly straightforward. British Airways operates the only direct flight from the UK to Bermuda, with one non-stop flight each day from London Heathrow (LHR) to Bermuda L.F. Wade International Airport (BDA)."
    linkCards={[
      { title: 'British Airways Flights to Bermuda', description: 'Search and book the direct London Heathrow to Bermuda route.', url: 'https://www.britishairways.com/nx/b/airselect/en/gbr/book/search/?trip=round&arrivalDate=2027-06-06&departureDate=2027-05-30&from=LHR&to=BDA&travelClass=economy&adults=1&youngAdults=0&children=0&infants=0&bound=outbound' },
      { title: 'British Airways Sale Page', description: 'Check for current British Airways sales and fare offers.', url: 'https://www.britishairways.com/content/offers/sale' },
      { title: 'Bermuda Online Visitor Form', description: 'Complete your arrival card online before you travel.', url: 'https://bermudaarrivalcard.com/' },
      { title: 'British Airways Low Fare Finder', description: 'Track fares across dates to find the best price.', url: 'https://www.britishairways.com/travel/low-price-finder/public/en_gb' },
      { title: 'ESTA Application', description: 'Required if you are flying via the United States.', url: 'https://esta.eta.travel/apply' },
    ]}
  >
    <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none font-sans text-navy/80 space-y-6">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl text-navy">British Airways</h2>
      <p>The outbound flight usually departs Heathrow in the mid-afternoon (around 2:30–3:00pm) and arrives in Bermuda at approximately 6:00pm local time. The return flight leaves Bermuda at around 7:45pm, flying overnight and arriving back at Heathrow at approximately 6:45am the following morning.</p>
      <p>Bermuda is 4 hours behind the UK in early June, helping to minimise jet lag.</p>

      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl text-navy">Typical Cost</h2>
      <p>Airfares to Bermuda vary considerably depending on when you book. As a guide, we'd generally expect the following for economy:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Lowest fares: from around £900 pp return (usually only available during sales or quieter booking periods).</li>
        <li>Typical fares: around £1,000–£1,200 pp return.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>At the time of writing, fares for June 2027 are towards the upper end of this range. This may simply reflect the initial release of tickets.</p>

      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl text-navy">When to Book</h2>
      <p>British Airways usually runs sales each year, most commonly in January, late spring/early summer (May–June) and around Black Friday (November).</p>
      <p>Our suggestion would be not to rush into booking at today's prices and keep an eye on fares over the coming months.</p>
      <p>The direct Bermuda flight has a relatively small Economy cabin and only operates once a day so we would avoid waiting until the last minute in case prices go up or if is sold out.</p>
      <p>We suggest using Google Flights to track prices for you.</p>

      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl text-navy">Travelling with infants</h2>
      <p>Children under the age of 2 can usually travel as a lap infant (without their own seat), subject to British Airways' infant fare. Once a child reaches their 2nd birthday, they will require their own seat.</p>

      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl text-navy">Flying via the United States</h2>
      <p>If you're looking to reduce the cost of your trip, flying via the United States can be much cheaper than taking the direct British Airways flight.</p>
      <p>Several US airlines operate regular services to Bermuda from major East Coast hubs, making it easy to connect from London or other UK airports.</p>
      <p>Popular routes include:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>New York (JFK) – John F. Kennedy International Airport – served by JetBlue Airways, Delta Air Lines and American Airlines</li>
        <li>Boston (BOS) – Logan International Airport – served by JetBlue Airways and Delta Air Lines</li>
        <li>Charlotte (CLT) – Charlotte Douglas International Airport – served by American Airlines</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl text-navy">Immigration</h2>
      <p>Bermuda is a British Overseas Territory so British Passport holders do not require a visa. You will just need to provide a completed arrival card to immigration when you arrive. These are available online at the <a href="https://bermudaarrivalcard.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="underline hover:text-navy">Bermuda Online Visitor Form</a>. Hard copies are also handed out during the flight.</p>
      <p>If flying via the United States then you will need an ESTA (even if you won't be leaving the airport).</p>
    </div>
  </InfoPage>
</BaseLayout>
